trol equipment; wired and wireless sensor wafers and reticles; wafer defect inspection, review, and metrology systems; reticle inspection and metrology systems; wafer inspection and metrology systems; semiconductor software solutions; KLA Pro systems; and specialty semiconductor manufacturing, benchtop metrology, surface characterization, material strength characterization, and electrical property measurement products. It also provides etch, plasma dicing, deposition and other wafer processing technologies and solutions; direct imaging, inspection, optical shaping, inkjet, and additive printing, as well as computer-aided manufacturing and engineering solutions; and components. In addition, the company offers service programs. It serves semiconductor, and semiconductor-related and electronic device manufacturers. The company operates in China, Taiwan, Korea, North America, Japan, Europe, Israel, and rest of Asia. The company was formerly known as KLA-Tencor Corporation and changed its name to KLA Corporation in July 2019. KLA Corporation was incorporated in 1975 and is headquartered in Milpitas, California.","employees":17000,"website":"https://www.kla.com","country":"United States","city":"Milpitas","officers":[{"name":"Mr. Richard P. Wallace","title":"President, CEO & Executive Director"},{"name":"Mr. Bren D. Higgins","title":"Executive VP & CFO"},{"name":"Ms. Mary Beth Wilkinson","title":"Executive VP, Chief Legal Officer & Corporate Secretary"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":17.28,"tpe":29.03,"ps":4.281,"pfcf":25.64,"peg":1.12,"pb":4.594,"ev_ebitda":18.59,"rev_growth":0.1935,"eps_growth":0.377,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2545,"eps_growth_next":0.1782,"div_yield":0,"roe":0.1242,"roa":0.05009,"de":32.04,"gross_margin":0.5374,"op_margin":0.1175,"profit_margin":0.09496,"current_ratio":1.852},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":21.2,"sector":17.28,"verdict":"Fairly valued"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":37.72,"sector":29.03,"verdict":"Overvalued"},{"k":"ps","label"